<title>GERMANY: Mercedes says Spanish plants hit by trucker strike.</title>
<headline>Mercedes says Spanish plants hit by trucker strike.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmaker Mercedes-Benz AG said on Monday that production at both of its Spanish plants had again been hit by an ongoing strike among Spanish lorry drivers.</p>
<p>A Mercedes spokesman said losses in production at its Vitoria plant since last Wednesday had meant that some 700 vehicles had not been built. The factory supplies the Vito transporters and the V-class limousines.</p>
<p>Production was also idle at its facility in Barcelona on Monday, according to the spokesman for Mercedes, a unit of industrial group Daimler-Benz AG.</p>
<p>Production at Mercedes' Duesseldorf plant, its only domestic plant which uses components from Spain, has not yet been affected by the strikes, he said, adding the plant had enough parts to maintain production through this week.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
